<h2>Concept and massing models</h2>
<p>Concept and massing models simplify a project into its primary volumes, heights, proportions, and site relationships.</p>
<p>They are commonly used during early design studies, internal reviews, planning discussions, and presentations where the overall design intent matters more than materials or façade details.</p>

<picture class="rs-photo" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;overflow:hidden;background:#111;border:1px solid var(--cm-border);margin:2rem 0 1.5rem;"><source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/rs-type-planning-4x3-480.avif 480w, /assets/rs-type-planning-4x3-800.avif 800w, /assets/rs-type-planning-4x3-1200.avif 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-planning-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-planning-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-planning-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><img src="/assets/rs-type-planning-4x3-1200.webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-planning-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-planning-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-planning-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Light wood massing model of a high-rise cluster used for design review" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"></picture>
<h2>Planning and design-review models</h2>
<p>Planning and design-review models help teams evaluate height, density, setbacks, circulation, neighboring context, public space, and the relationship between a proposal and its surroundings.</p>
<p>They can support planning applications, entitlement discussions, community presentations, stakeholder reviews, and internal design decisions.</p>

<picture class="rs-photo" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;overflow:hidden;background:#111;border:1px solid var(--cm-border);margin:2rem 0 1.5rem;"><source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/rs-type-masterplan-v2-4x3-480.avif 480w, /assets/rs-type-masterplan-v2-4x3-800.avif 800w, /assets/rs-type-masterplan-v2-4x3-1200.avif 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-masterplan-v2-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-masterplan-v2-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-masterplan-v2-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><img src="/assets/rs-type-masterplan-v2-4x3-1200.webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-masterplan-v2-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-masterplan-v2-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-masterplan-v2-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Masterplan model of a green residential district with white buildings, roads and landscaping" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"></picture>
<h2>Masterplan and urban-planning models</h2>
<p>Masterplan models represent larger developments containing multiple buildings, streets, open spaces, infrastructure, and landscape.</p>
<p>They help audiences understand development phases, circulation, density, site organization, and relationships that may be difficult to interpret from plans or individual renderings.</p>

<picture class="rs-photo" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;overflow:hidden;background:#111;border:1px solid var(--cm-border);margin:2rem 0 1.5rem;"><source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/rs-type-presentation-4x3-480.avif 480w, /assets/rs-type-presentation-4x3-800.avif 800w, /assets/rs-type-presentation-4x3-1200.avif 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-presentation-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-presentation-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-presentation-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><img src="/assets/rs-type-presentation-4x3-1200.webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-presentation-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-presentation-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-presentation-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Sales gallery architectural model of two curved glass towers inside a showroom atrium" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"></picture>
<h2>Presentation and sales-gallery models</h2>
<p>Presentation models communicate a developed design through carefully selected architectural detail, materials, glazing, landscaping, lighting, and finishes.</p>
<p>They are commonly used for investor meetings, client presentations, sales galleries, marketing environments, public exhibitions, and other situations where the model must communicate clearly and create a strong physical presence.</p>

<picture class="rs-photo" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;overflow:hidden;background:#111;border:1px solid var(--cm-border);margin:2rem 0 1.5rem;"><source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/rs-type-topo-4x3-480.avif 480w, /assets/rs-type-topo-4x3-800.avif 800w, /assets/rs-type-topo-4x3-1200.avif 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-topo-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-topo-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-topo-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><img src="/assets/rs-type-topo-4x3-1200.webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-topo-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-topo-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-topo-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Topographic site model of a mountain landscape with a labeled hillside" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"></picture>
<h2>Topographic and site models</h2>
<p>Topographic models show terrain, contours, water, roads, vegetation, site boundaries, and the relationship between a project and its natural or constructed context.</p>
<p>They are useful for landscape design, hillside development, infrastructure planning, environmental review, site analysis, and presentation.</p>

<picture class="rs-photo" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;overflow:hidden;background:#111;border:1px solid var(--cm-border);margin:2rem 0 1.5rem;"><source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/rs-type-interior-4x3-480.avif 480w, /assets/rs-type-interior-4x3-800.avif 800w, /assets/rs-type-interior-4x3-1200.avif 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-interior-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-interior-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-interior-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><img src="/assets/rs-type-interior-4x3-1200.webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-interior-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-interior-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-interior-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Interior section model of a theater with curved red seating and layered white walls" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"></picture>
<h2>Interior and section models</h2>
<p>Interior models represent rooms, units, floors, or larger interior environments. Section models reveal spatial relationships that would otherwise remain hidden inside the building.</p>
<p>They can help audiences understand circulation, ceiling heights, structure, program relationships, furniture, finishes, and the experience of moving through a space.</p>

<picture class="rs-photo" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;overflow:hidden;background:#111;border:1px solid var(--cm-border);margin:2rem 0 1.5rem;"><source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/rs-type-construction-4x3-480.avif 480w, /assets/rs-type-construction-4x3-800.avif 800w, /assets/rs-type-construction-4x3-1200.avif 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-construction-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-construction-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-construction-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><img src="/assets/rs-type-construction-4x3-1200.webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-construction-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-construction-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-construction-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Construction coordination model with excavators, dump trucks and gravel on a site" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"></picture>
<h2>Coordination and construction models</h2>
<p>Coordination models isolate important assemblies, structural relationships, construction sequences, access conditions, or technically complex areas.</p>
<p>They can help design and construction teams communicate proposed solutions, review buildability, coordinate stakeholders, and prepare for fabrication or installation.</p>

<picture class="rs-photo" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;overflow:hidden;background:#111;border:1px solid var(--cm-border);margin:2rem 0 1.5rem;"><source type="image/avif" srcset="/assets/rs-type-asbuilt-4x3-480.avif 480w, /assets/rs-type-asbuilt-4x3-800.avif 800w, /assets/rs-type-asbuilt-4x3-1200.avif 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-asbuilt-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-asbuilt-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-asbuilt-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px"><img src="/assets/rs-type-asbuilt-4x3-1200.webp" srcset="/assets/rs-type-asbuilt-4x3-480.webp 480w, /assets/rs-type-asbuilt-4x3-800.webp 800w, /assets/rs-type-asbuilt-4x3-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 92vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Illuminated cutaway model of a multi-storey modern house with a rooftop pool" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;"></picture>
<h2>Existing-condition and as-built models</h2>
<p>Existing-condition models document a building, site, facility, or piece of infrastructure as it currently exists.</p>
<p>They may be used for renovation planning, facility communication, exhibitions, stakeholder presentations, fundraising, historical documentation, or as a physical record of a completed project.</p>

<h2>How do you choose the right type?</h2>
<p>Begin with three questions:</p>
<ul>
<li>Who will use or view the model?</li>
<li>What do they need to understand?</li>
<li>What decision, presentation, evaluation, or approval must the model support?</li>
</ul>
<p>The answers determine the appropriate model type, <a href="/blog/how-to-choose-architectural-model-scale">scale</a>, boundaries, level of detail, materials, lighting, and presentation requirements.</p>
<p>A planning model and a sales-gallery model may represent the same development, but they do not necessarily need to show the same information. Defining the purpose before selecting the details produces a clearer and more effective model.</p>
